1
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,834
Hey! Hey, you!

2
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:28,751
Well, my feelings are
you're a two-time louse,

3
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:31,229
just like all the rest of them.

4
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:33,309
What's going on here?

5
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:36,438
At the moment, you're interrupting
Mrs. Sutcliffe's session, Mr. Cassidy.

6
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:38,113
What's the problem?

7
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:43,032
I took three connecting flights
on three different airlines to get here.

8
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:45,395
Nobody but you people
are supposed to know I'm here.

9
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,391
- No one does.
- Oh, yeah?

10
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:50,313
What about the photographer
I caught sneaking around my suite?

11
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:52,472
I'll notify Security.

12
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:55,791
Brett Cassidy, the movie star?
Oh, I'm a great admirer of yours.

13
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:58,713
I rarely go to movies,
but I've seen most of your pictures.

14
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:00,029
Barbara Sutcliffe.

15
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:03,351
All right, Mr. Cassidy, if you'll go
to your suite, I'll contact Security,

16
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:06,114
and I'm sure
they'll check everything out, okay?

17
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:10,239
Listen to me, you guaranteed me
my confidentiality and my privacy.

18
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:12,516
We'll talk about that
during your session.

19
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,798
Would you like me to escort you
back to your suite?

20
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:21,509
- No, I think I can find it, thank you.
- It was nice meeting you.

21
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:28,317
- Can I help you, Mr. Patterson?
- I'm next.

22
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:30,835
Isn't that that movie actor,
what's-his-name?

23
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,468
- That's him.
- That's what I thought.

24
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:37,872
- He's not as tall as you'd expect.
- They never are.

25
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,718
Excuse me?

26
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:22,277
Excuse me?

27
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:25,512
- Hello?
- Mr. Matlock.

28
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:27,673
Mr. Matlock.

29
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:30,115
The janitor let me in.

30
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:34,150
I must've fallen asleep. I was awake
all night on the bus, then I came here.

31
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:35,639
Excuse me.

32
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:40,278
- Do I know you?
- Cassie. Cassie Phillips from Chicago.

33
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:42,074
Chicago?

34
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:45,118
You gave a lecture there
at the university last March.

35
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:49,114
I remember that.
What can I do for you?

36
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:51,630
Well, I'm here about the job.

37
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:53,669
What job?

38
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:57,276
The one you promised me in Chicago,
as your assistant.

39
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:59,556
- Assistant?
- Right after the lecture,

40
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:02,280
I interviewed you
for the school paper.

41
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:04,309
My shoes.

42
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:07,631
I took them off when I began to nap
while I was waiting for you to come in.

43
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,711
Don't take that as a criticism,
because it's not.

44
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:12,394
I mean, a lot of people in your position
start work late.

45
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:14,434
Miss Phillips,

46
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:17,319
I think we have
a serious misunderstanding here.

47
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:20,438
- We do?
- I don't know who you are.

48
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:23,193
Well, I sent you a registered letter.

49
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:29,233
Where's my purse? Excuse me.
I know I kept the receipt.

50
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:33,517
I don't remember
offering you any employment.

51
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:41,911
Well, I looked different then.
I had pink hair, remember?

52
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:45,396
Oh, with all those little things
in your ear?

53
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:48,074
Yeah. Well,
when I decided to become a lawyer,

54
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:51,312
well, I obviously needed a new look.

55
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,756
- You graduated?
- Yes.

56
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:55,558
- From the university?
- Yes.

57
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:59,235
I just enrolled at Baxter Law School.
And that's why I'm so grateful to you,

58
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,960
because Baxter requires
all its first-year students to be interns.

59
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:03,917
And so when I told--

60
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:06,275
Oh, so Baxter let you in

61
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:09,000
because they think
you're working for me?

62
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,752
Yes.

63
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,672
How did that happen?

64
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:15,915
I wrote it on my application.

65
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:20,716
Miss Phillips, you actually told them
you had a job here?

66
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:23,599
- Well, I'm sorry--
- You mean you won't give me a job?

67
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:26,513
- There's no job to give.
- But what about that empty office?

68
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:28,830
It's not empty.
That's my daughter Charlene's office.

69
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,673
She's in Philadelphia right now
working on a case.

70
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:34,597
Miss Phillips,

71
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:37,436
there is no job.

72
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:41,798
I don't know
how I can say it any plainer.

73
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:44,951
I'm sorry.

74
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:51,790
Well, I guess
it was just a misunderstanding, huh?

75
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:55,352
I guess so.

76
00:06:57,080 --> 00:07:00,993
Well, I guess
I don't have to go to law school.

77
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:03,674
I mean, a girl my age
has lots of options.

78
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:06,151
Lots of them.

79
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:08,392
Listen, thanks anyway.

80
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:11,996
I'm sure this was all my fault.
I must have assumed too much.

81
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:15,277
You know how impulsive
young people can be. They--

82
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:17,476
They get inspired
by someone like yourself.

83
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:20,200
They wanna model themselves
after them.

84
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:22,271
Get carried away.

85
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:28,955
Nice seeing you again. Bye.

86
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:34,756
Wait a minute.

87
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:44,917
I suppose
there are some odds and ends

88
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:48,834
that could be done around here.

89
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:53,949
Filing things and taking things
to the courthouse and...

90
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:57,510
Only temporary,
till you find yourself a new position.

91
00:07:57,680 --> 00:08:00,319
Oh, thank you.
I really appreciate this.

92
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:03,035
Put your things in Charlene's office
for now.

93
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:06,431
Oh, they're already in there.
I'll get started right away.

94
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,838
Are you free for lunch?

95
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,228
No.

96
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:18,589
No problem.
I'll be in here, if you need me.

97
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:21,957
And if you change your mind
about lunch.

98
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:27,479
<i>--final, 1 1 1- 1 1 0.</i>

99
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:28,959
<i>And that's it for sports.</i>

100
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:31,918
<i>Bonnie McGrath's up next</i>
<i>with entertainment. Bonnie?</i>

101
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:34,469
<i>And do we have news tonight.</i>

102
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:38,519
<i>Women of Atlanta, hold on tight,</i>
<i>because guess who's come to town.</i>

103
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:40,193
<i>Anonymous sources tell us</i>

104
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:43,352
<i>that heartthrob star of stage</i>
<i>and screen Brett Cassidy</i>

105
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:45,750
<i>is making a pit stop</i>
<i>at the Halvern Clinic,</i>

106
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:48,992
<i>nationally known sex clinic</i>
<i>here in Atlanta.</i>

107
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:52,197
What's his problem?
Well, we don't know yet.

108
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:55,432
But the way we hear it,
the quarterback of romance

109
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:58,910
<i>may be having trouble</i>
<i>scoring that winning touchdown.</i>

110
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:02,959
<i>More on this story</i>
<i>as the juicy details become available.</i>

111
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:05,395
<i>In other entertainment--</i>

112
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:09,238
Okay, Halvern,
this has gone far enough...

113
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:48,074
I don't know.
I guess the person that took my picture

114
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:50,913
could've been working
for the TV station.

115
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:53,514
But I don't understand
how they knew I was at the clinic.

116
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:54,954
Dr. Halvern assured me

117
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:58,556
that all the patients were registered
under fictitious names.

118
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:03,077
I don't get it. I don't get it.
I don't understand any of it.

119
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:06,239
That's a real puzzle, isn't it?

120
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:09,632
- Who are you?
- I'm Mr. Matlock's assistant.

121
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:12,792
So you didn't notice
that your isometric bar was missing?

122
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:15,349
No, I didn't.
I don't carry it with me all the time.

123
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:17,351
- Are you an attorney?
- Not exactly.

124
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:19,750
So someone could've taken it
during your session

125
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:22,195
- when you didn't have it with you?
- That's possible.

126
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:25,193
If you're not an attorney, why are you
asking me all these questions?

127
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:28,716
I told you,
I'm Mr. Matlock's assistant.

128
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:32,479
Am I interrupting something?

129
00:10:33,680 --> 00:10:35,955
Oh, hi.

130
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:39,270
This is Ben Matlock.

131
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:43,274
This is Brett Cassidy.
You know, from Hollywood.

132
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:45,870
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you.

133
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:47,509
Mr. Cassidy was here early,

134
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:51,514
so I thought we'd get some
of the preliminaries out of the way.

135
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,156
Would you just excuse us
for a moment?

136
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:59,392
It was a pleasure meeting you,
Mr. Cassidy.

137
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:04,353
What do you think you're doing?

138
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:07,034
Getting a statement about what
happened the night of the murder.

139
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,633
Shall I give it to you from the top?

140
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:11,109
- I know all about it.
- You do?

141
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:14,158
Sam Young told me this morning
down at the jail.

142
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:17,114
- Who's Sam Young?
- His local counsel.

143
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:18,872
Cassie,

144
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:22,991
I'm not the new kid on the block.
You are.

145
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:28,319
Yeah. Well, I guess
I could type these notes out for the file.

146
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:32,758
Yeah, do that. Type them up, file them,
file this stuff, file everything.

147
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:37,152
And after you've filed everything,
go through the classifieds.

148
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:39,470
I'll handle the case.
You're not my assistant.

149
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:43,872
You're just here temporarily
till you find another job, remember?

150
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:48,116
The classifieds.

151
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:51,236
Couldn't I do it
after Mr. Cassidy leaves?

152
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:55,075
I could sort of stand silently by
and take notes while you ques--

153
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:57,800
- Cassie.
- The classifieds.

154
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:03,112
He has no idea
who stole his isometric bar.

155
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:04,349
Classifieds.

156
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:11,598
So...

157
00:12:11,760 --> 00:12:13,796
Sam Young arrange your bail?

158
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:17,953
That's right. Said you were
the best defence attorney in town.

159
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:20,512
Did he say I don't work for free?

160
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:22,274
Money's no problem.

161
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:26,956
Well, you don't look like you've missed
too many Thanksgivings.

162
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:28,712
What happened out there?

163
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:31,553
Well, I had my session
with Dr. Halvern in the morning,

164
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:34,678
went back to see him last night,
he was dead.

165
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:37,551
District attorney
says he has witnesses

166
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:39,915
that you had an argument
with Dr. Halvern.

167
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:43,272
Dr. Halvern assured me that
no one would know I was at the clinic.

168
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:44,475
Then this local TV vulture

169
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:47,632
uses me as the cover story
for the evening news.

170
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:50,596
Well, where were you
at the time of the murder?

171
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:53,076
- In my suite.
- Alone?

172
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,229
That's right.

173
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:57,472
You're not allowed to bring anybody
with you when you stay at the clinic.

174
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:59,073
Why not?

175
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,912
You're just not.

176
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:02,594
Yeah, but why not?

177
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:08,399
Well, you see, the idea
is to cleanse the mind and the body,

178
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:11,870
remove yourself from the day-to-day
life pressures while you're there,

179
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:15,112
so when you go back,
you can function better.

180
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:17,874
Function better?

181
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:20,270
That's right, function better.

182
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:23,790
I have one other question.
Did you do it?

183
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:26,428
- Do what?
- Kill Dr. Halvern.

184
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:29,232
No, sir, I didn't.

185
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:33,357
- Okay, you got a lawyer.
- Thank you.

186
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:36,114
Now, just curious,
this ''functioning better'' part,

187
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:38,794
what exactly goes on
in those sessions?

188
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:41,110
I don't wanna talk about it.

189
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:43,398
I didn't mean to press.

190
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:49,996
This is where
the guard found Dr. Halvern.

191
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:59,197
There doesn't appear
to have been much of a struggle.

192
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:04,037
Were you the last person
to see Dr. Halvern alive?

193
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:06,111
No, he had a patient at 7:00.

194
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:08,510
- Who was that?
- Mrs. Barbara Sutcliffe.

195
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:11,593
This Mrs. Sutcliffe was here
till 8:00?

196
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:13,398
She would've left
ten minutes before that.

197
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:15,630
The standard therapy hour
is 50 minutes.

198
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:18,360
The 50-minute hour.
It allows the doctor time to make notes

199
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:20,272
and organise his thoughts
between patients.

200
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:21,998
Right.

201
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:23,475
You wanted to see me?

202
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:26,552
Mr. Matlock, this is Alex Fenton.
He was on duty that night.

203
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:29,154
- Mr. Fenton, you a doctor?
- Oh, no, no. I'm a technician.

204
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:30,799
I take care of the equipment.

205
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:34,714
- What equipment?
- The video and other equipment.

206
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,594
Dr. Halvern
recorded all his sessions.

207
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:54,232
Well, didn't that
make his patients uncomfortable?

208
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:56,550
They didn't know.

209
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:57,755
Thank you, Alex.

210
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:02,472
What happens to the clinic
now that Dr. Halvern's dead?

211
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:04,198
It hasn't been decided yet.

212
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,275
You were engaged to him at one time,
weren't you?

213
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:09,473
That was a long time ago.

214
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:13,750
It's a shame you didn't marry.
This would've been yours.

215
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:15,878
One last question.

216
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:18,554
I was in my office
writing reports alone.

217
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:20,957
Well, thank you.

218
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:33,549
Thank God you're here.

219
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:37,156
Now, there are these two
and there's a suitcase in the bedroom.

220
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:41,833
If you want a tip,
you'd better get moving.

221
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,353
I'm sorry, Mrs. Sutcliffe,

222
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:45,158
but I'm afraid
we're not going anywhere.

223
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:46,912
- Well, what's this?
- That is a subpoena.

224
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:48,195
And you can keep the change.

225
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:51,158
But you can't do this.
I've got a plane to catch.

226
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:53,788
I'm sorry, but we're gonna need you
to testify at the trial.

227
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:55,188
Why do you need me?

228
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:57,112
Aren't they going to
convict Brett Cassidy?

229
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:59,555
We're defending him.

230
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,796
- These belong to you?
- No. No.

231
00:16:07,960 --> 00:16:09,188
No? I didn't think so.

232
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:12,079
Didn't look like the kind of key ring
that you would have.

233
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:14,278
See you at the trial.

234
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:25,039
- Yeah?
- Hi. You Josh Patterson?

235
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:27,555
- Who wants to know?
- Special delivery.

236
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:29,790
- What's this?
- It's a subpoena.

237
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,871
What'd you come up with?

238
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:56,236
Barbara Sutcliffe,
she's a regular at the clinic.

239
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:57,594
She's been married five times.

240
00:16:57,760 --> 00:16:59,751
She checks in there
after every divorce.

241
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:02,880
You think she just gets tired of them,
or there's something wrong?

242
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:04,996
You know,
there's nothing happening.

243
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:07,230
Or maybe
she just likes to move around?

244
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:09,514
Could be.

245
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:12,278
What about Josh Patterson?

246
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:15,000
Yeah, what about Josh Patterson?
What's wrong with him?

247
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:16,149
I don't know.

248
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:17,958
Well, what do they do
in those sessions?

249
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,109
I'm not sure.

250
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:23,876
Talk about whether they're tense
or nervous or unsure, I guess.

251
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,712
You ever been
to one of these places?

252
00:17:27,760 --> 00:17:28,909
No. Have you?

253
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:31,353
Not until now.

254
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,638
Well, what about Josh Patterson?

255
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:37,758
You told me the patients at the clinic
were supposed to stay there alone.

256
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:39,638
- Yeah.
- Well, he wasn't.

257
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:43,236
I saw someone else in his suite,
and I swear it looked like a woman.

258
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:45,914
Do you think
that's part of the therapy?

259
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:47,548
Might not hurt.

260
00:17:49,080 --> 00:17:50,911
Why don't you see
if you can find out who it is?

261
00:17:51,080 --> 00:17:53,799
- I'm on my way.
- Yeah.

262
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,558
Yeah?

263
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:41,517
- Evening, Joshua.
- Did Jennifer tell you I was here?

264
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:44,717
Or did that creep Halvern
call you too?

265
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:53,593
My daughter suspects you're sleeping
with some broad, and she's right.

266
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:57,275
I'm here
to try and save my marriage.

267
00:18:58,280 --> 00:19:00,191
What was that?

268
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:18,355
Clean up your act, boy,
or I'll clean it up for you.

269
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:20,397
Now, get out of here.

270
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:50,031
Oh, hi.

271
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:54,233
What are you doing?

272
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:56,152
Well, I thought
I'd rearrange these law books

273
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:57,912
and put them in chronological order.

274
00:19:58,080 --> 00:20:01,038
I hoped I'd be done before you got in,
because I wanted to surprise you.

275
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:03,919
Cassie,
I'm not looking for any surprises.

276
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:07,432
I had these books arranged
according to my own system.

277
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:10,239
Civil law over there,
criminal law over here.

278
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:12,789
Well, I'm not sure that I can
put them back the way they were,

279
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:16,316
because I didn't pay too much attention
to the way they were.

280
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:19,358
I'm very particular
about the way I like things,

281
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:21,715
and I very much liked things
the way they were.

282
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:26,475
And I like the music the way it was.

283
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,117
Did you file those petitions
at the courthouse?

284
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:32,555
No, not yet,
but have I got news for you.

285
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:35,439
Cassie, those papers
have to be in by today.

286
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:37,431
I'll do it.
Do you remember Bonnie McGrath,

287
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:40,160
the TV announcer who did the piece
on Brett Cassidy at the clinic?

288
00:20:40,320 --> 00:20:42,880
Well, the person who tipped her
was a woman.

289
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:44,555
How do you know?

290
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:47,109
Because I went to the TV station
and I asked her.

291
00:20:51,040 --> 00:20:52,234
We have a problem.

292
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:53,992
I figure that the person
who tipped Bonnie

293
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:56,674
is probably the same person
who set Brett up for the murder.

294
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:58,432
That's not the problem.

295
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:01,319
Oh, I know I should've
filed your motions before I went.

296
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:03,869
That's not the problem.
You're a law student.

297
00:21:04,040 --> 00:21:06,600
You're not supposed to be working
on these cases.

298
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,479
Well, I was just trying to help.

299
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:11,999
Cassie, you can't go around
asking people questions

300
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:14,151
when you have no idea
how they'll react.

301
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:15,309
This is not a game.

302
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:19,314
Ben, once again,
I am the bearer of good news.

303
00:21:19,840 --> 00:21:21,671
Excuse me,
am I interrupting something?

304
00:21:21,840 --> 00:21:23,558
Tyler, this is Cassie Phillips.

305
00:21:23,720 --> 00:21:27,599
She's a filer. She files things.
She's a temporary filer.

306
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:29,830
This is Tyler Hudson.
He's an investigator.

307
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:33,197
He's the one who goes around
and asks people questions, okay?

308
00:21:33,360 --> 00:21:34,554
- Okay.
- What's the good news?

309
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:37,757
All right, I paid a visit to Mr. Patterson,
and there is a woman in his suite,

310
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:39,273
but it's not his wife.

311
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:41,908
Josh Patterson
is married to Jennifer Gellar,

312
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:43,433
the daughter of Big John Gellar,

313
00:21:43,600 --> 00:21:46,160
as you may remember,
the centimillionaire out of Houston.

314
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:48,834
Now, take a look at this.
That's Mrs. Patterson.

315
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:51,116
The woman out at the clinic
is 20 pounds lighter

316
00:21:51,280 --> 00:21:53,714
and 1 0 years younger.

317
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:01,077
I'll go on and file some things.

318
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:05,635
Better get a subpoena

319
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:07,392
on Mr. Patterson's lady friend
right away.

320
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:08,549
Okay.

321
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:10,438
It was a woman
who tipped the TV station

322
00:22:10,600 --> 00:22:11,919
that Brett was at the clinic.

323
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:14,389
Now, how do we know that?

324
00:22:15,480 --> 00:22:16,913
- Cassie.
- Who is she?

325
00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:19,913
I don't know. She showed up here
the other day looking for work,

326
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:22,674
and I was trying to help her out,
but every time I turn my back,

327
00:22:22,840 --> 00:22:25,115
she's into everything.

328
00:22:25,280 --> 00:22:28,750
Maybe if I keep her with me,
she'll stay out of trouble.

329
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:30,558
Lay a subpoena on that dame
out there.

330
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:32,312
You got it.

331
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:34,916
Get your coat. We're--

332
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:20,191
- Who are you?
- I wanna talk to you.

333
00:23:20,360 --> 00:23:25,388
No. You get out of here right now
or I'm gonna call Security.

334
00:23:25,560 --> 00:23:27,357
You can't do that.

335
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:30,270
You're not supposed to be here.

336
00:23:38,040 --> 00:23:40,759
- What do you want?
- I work for Ben Matlock.

337
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:44,469
He's Brett Cassidy's attorney.
And I'd like to ask you a few questions.

338
00:23:44,640 --> 00:23:46,437
I'm not gonna answer any questions.

339
00:23:46,600 --> 00:23:48,875
I think it would be better all around
if you did.

340
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:50,839
Do you have a subpoena?

341
00:23:52,080 --> 00:23:55,629
Actually,
I don't happen to have one on me.

342
00:23:55,800 --> 00:23:57,995
Why don't we just assume
that I have one?

343
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:03,309
Can't we just talk this over informally,
woman-to-woman?

344
00:24:03,480 --> 00:24:06,438
- You know, like that?
- Why?

345
00:24:06,600 --> 00:24:09,478
- Because my life is a mess.
- What?

346
00:24:09,640 --> 00:24:11,471
My life is a mess.

347
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:17,235
See, I work for Ben Matlock,
but it's only temporary, very temporary,

348
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:20,551
unless I can show him
that I can really make a contribution.

349
00:24:20,720 --> 00:24:23,678
And if I don't,
well, I'm out of his office,

350
00:24:23,840 --> 00:24:27,276
I'm out of law school,
and I'm generally out of luck.

351
00:24:27,440 --> 00:24:28,429
So I was hoping

352
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:33,230
that maybe you could just answer
one or two very small questions.

353
00:24:34,320 --> 00:24:35,719
Like what?

354
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:39,631
Like, why are you here
with a married man?

355
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:52,914
At first,
I didn't know he was married.

356
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:56,675
I mean, he didn't mention it
and I didn't ask.

357
00:24:56,840 --> 00:24:58,273
Look, I know I shouldn't be here.

358
00:24:58,440 --> 00:25:02,718
I should get out of here right now,
but he wants me here,

359
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:05,440
and he's so hard to refuse.

360
00:25:07,280 --> 00:25:11,512
- Does that answer your question?
- I had two.

361
00:25:13,360 --> 00:25:14,588
Okay.

362
00:25:15,080 --> 00:25:17,435
Where were you
when Dr. Halvern was murdered?

363
00:25:17,600 --> 00:25:19,397
Right here with Josh.

364
00:25:20,120 --> 00:25:23,271
All night? I mean,
you're sure he was here all night?

365
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:24,959
Let's just put it this way:

366
00:25:25,120 --> 00:25:28,112
Neither one of us
really needs any therapy.

367
00:25:31,040 --> 00:25:32,837
Then why come here?

368
00:25:34,040 --> 00:25:37,919
It's quiet. Place to hide out.

369
00:25:48,280 --> 00:25:49,349
Oh, no.

370
00:25:49,520 --> 00:25:51,715
Those guys,
they work for Josh's father-in-law.

371
00:25:51,880 --> 00:25:55,236
Well, get in the bedroom.
I'll take care of it.

372
00:25:58,120 --> 00:26:01,112
- Kimberly Bradshaw?
- She's not in at the moment.

373
00:26:02,200 --> 00:26:04,430
Fellas, please. Where are we going?

374
00:26:19,960 --> 00:26:21,632
Hey.

375
00:26:23,160 --> 00:26:24,718
Hey, wait a minute!

376
00:26:31,480 --> 00:26:33,596
Mrs. Sutcliffe,

377
00:26:34,040 --> 00:26:36,270
you've been a patient
at the Halvern Clinic

378
00:26:36,440 --> 00:26:37,759
for the past two weeks.

379
00:26:37,920 --> 00:26:39,990
- Is that correct?
- Yes, it is.

380
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:43,436
And you were a patient there
five times before. Is that correct?

381
00:26:43,600 --> 00:26:46,990
Yes. Dr. Halvern
helped me through my divorces.

382
00:26:47,160 --> 00:26:49,310
- How?
- Just talking.

383
00:26:49,480 --> 00:26:51,152
I see.

384
00:26:52,080 --> 00:26:55,356
- Do you own a home at Hilton Head?
- I do.

385
00:26:55,520 --> 00:27:00,196
Did Dr. Halvern stay with you
at your home in Hilton Head

386
00:27:00,360 --> 00:27:03,989
this past July,
the 1 5th through the 22nd?

387
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:05,195
Yes.

388
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:07,430
And do you own a cabin
in the Berkshires,

389
00:27:07,600 --> 00:27:11,479
where you and Dr. Halvern
spent two weeks last December?

390
00:27:11,640 --> 00:27:12,629
Yes.

391
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:18,113
Mrs. Sutcliffe, isn't it true that you
and Dr. Halvern were having an affair?

392
00:27:19,800 --> 00:27:26,239
It's-- It's not exactly a secret,
Miss Sutcliffe.

393
00:27:26,400 --> 00:27:28,470
Yes, we were having an affair.

394
00:27:29,280 --> 00:27:33,034
And isn't it true
that you recently found out

395
00:27:33,200 --> 00:27:37,671
that Dr. Halvern was stepping out
on you, seeing other women

396
00:27:37,840 --> 00:27:40,559
at the same time
he was involved with you?

397
00:27:40,720 --> 00:27:41,709
Yes.

398
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:44,750
So this man whom you trusted

399
00:27:44,920 --> 00:27:48,276
and to whom you told
your deepest secrets

400
00:27:48,440 --> 00:27:50,749
was deceiving you, wasn't he?

401
00:27:50,920 --> 00:27:53,753
- Yes.
- It made you very angry, didn't it?

402
00:27:53,920 --> 00:27:55,478
Yes.

403
00:27:56,680 --> 00:28:02,994
I call your attention to this set of keys
marked ''Halvern,''

404
00:28:03,160 --> 00:28:08,075
and each key is numbered
consecutively 1 through 20

405
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:09,958
with this charm.

406
00:28:10,120 --> 00:28:13,112
- Do you recognise them?
- I don't know.

407
00:28:13,280 --> 00:28:15,271
My investigator found them
in your bungalow.

408
00:28:15,440 --> 00:28:16,475
So?

409
00:28:16,640 --> 00:28:20,315
Well, these keys open all the doors
at the clinic.

410
00:28:20,480 --> 00:28:22,436
What were they doing
in your bungalow?

411
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:26,479
Well, I suppose the technician,
Mr. Fenton,

412
00:28:26,640 --> 00:28:29,359
must've left them there
when he came by to repair my TV.

413
00:28:29,520 --> 00:28:32,080
The cable on my TV.

414
00:28:32,240 --> 00:28:33,878
What's so special about them?

415
00:28:34,440 --> 00:28:37,477
Well, with these keys,

416
00:28:37,640 --> 00:28:40,916
you could've unlocked the door
to Brett Cassidy's suite,

417
00:28:41,080 --> 00:28:42,798
stolen his isometric bar,

418
00:28:42,960 --> 00:28:46,589
and since you were Dr. Halvern's
last patient the night of the murder,

419
00:28:47,760 --> 00:28:50,399
you could've entered the therapy room
without knocking.

420
00:28:50,560 --> 00:28:53,120
- Objection.
- Sustained.

421
00:28:54,960 --> 00:28:56,871
Where were you
at the time of the murder?

422
00:28:57,040 --> 00:28:58,473
- In my cottage.
- Alone?

423
00:28:58,640 --> 00:29:01,871
No, Mr. Fenton came by
to fix the cable on my TV.

424
00:29:02,040 --> 00:29:05,032
Mrs. Sutcliffe,
it can't have taken Mr. Fenton

425
00:29:05,200 --> 00:29:08,192
more than ten minutes
to fix the cable on your TV.

426
00:29:08,360 --> 00:29:09,793
It didn't.

427
00:29:09,960 --> 00:29:12,235
Well, what time
did Mr. Fenton leave?

428
00:29:12,400 --> 00:29:13,958
Nine a.m.

429
00:29:14,840 --> 00:29:16,512
Nine a.m.?

430
00:29:18,120 --> 00:29:20,475
Alex and I have known each other
for almost ten years,

431
00:29:20,640 --> 00:29:25,236
but I'd never realised what a kind
and tender man he really is.

432
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:29,712
When Carl was murdered,
I was with Alex, Mr. Matlock.

433
00:29:29,880 --> 00:29:34,396
- Is he going to be your next husband?
- Well, as a matter of fact, yes.

434
00:29:35,320 --> 00:29:37,959
Congratulations.
No further questions.

435
00:29:38,120 --> 00:29:41,795
In view of the hour, court is in recess
until 1 0 a.m. tomorrow.

436
00:29:41,960 --> 00:29:45,430
- Thought I had her there for a second.
- Oh, you were doing good for a while.

437
00:29:45,600 --> 00:29:49,115
- Well, there's always tomorrow.
- Yeah, I'm glad about that.

438
00:29:55,760 --> 00:29:59,196
- Ben, Cassie's been kidnapped.
- What are you talking about?

439
00:29:59,360 --> 00:30:02,352
Two guys forced her into a limo
out at the clinic and drove away.

440
00:30:02,520 --> 00:30:05,478
- What was she doing at the clinic?
- I didn't have time to ask.

441
00:30:06,760 --> 00:30:09,479
Go down to Headquarters and get
Lieutenant Daniels on this right away.

442
00:30:09,640 --> 00:30:11,790
I'll go to the office
to see if anybody left a message.

443
00:30:11,960 --> 00:30:13,439
You got it.

444
00:30:21,680 --> 00:30:23,989
<i>Dad?</i>
<i>I just called to see how you were.</i>

445
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:25,673
<i>Everything's great here.</i>

446
00:30:42,080 --> 00:30:45,152
Lieutenant Daniels, please.
This is an emergency.

447
00:30:49,120 --> 00:30:50,678
Hello?

448
00:30:53,040 --> 00:30:54,632
Who's there?

449
00:30:57,720 --> 00:31:00,996
- Are you all right?
- Perfect.

450
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:04,038
I've got the police looking for you.
I thought you were kidnapped.

451
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:06,077
Where have you been?

452
00:31:06,520 --> 00:31:08,590
It's all in my report.

453
00:31:09,600 --> 00:31:12,160
Oh, I filed your motions
at the courthouse.

454
00:31:12,320 --> 00:31:14,595
Then I went out to the clinic
and I saw Kimberly Bradshaw,

455
00:31:14,760 --> 00:31:16,637
the girl staying
in Josh Patterson's bungalow.

456
00:31:16,800 --> 00:31:18,791
Well, Big John's bodyguards
thought I was Kimberly,

457
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:20,632
so they kidnapped me
instead of Kimberly.

458
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:23,314
I told Big John that Kimberly
didn't know that Josh was married

459
00:31:23,480 --> 00:31:26,392
and she knows this will never work.
He turned out to be a very nice man.

460
00:31:26,560 --> 00:31:29,552
He's giving Kimberly
a plane ticket home to Burbank.

461
00:31:29,720 --> 00:31:32,234
Yeah, that's where she lives,
Burbank.

462
00:31:32,800 --> 00:31:36,270
He's giving her a monthly allowance
to help her get back on her feet.

463
00:31:36,440 --> 00:31:38,954
Oh, and I forgot
to type in the most important part:

464
00:31:39,120 --> 00:31:41,918
Kimberly and Josh Patterson have
an alibi for the time of the murder.

465
00:31:42,080 --> 00:31:45,789
They were together.
They don't need therapy.

466
00:31:47,320 --> 00:31:50,198
So we can eliminate them
as suspects.

467
00:31:53,080 --> 00:31:55,913
So can people start calling me
your assistant?

468
00:31:56,080 --> 00:31:58,116
You know, a regular job?

469
00:32:01,840 --> 00:32:05,719
I told you the first day,

470
00:32:06,560 --> 00:32:08,232
there is no job.

471
00:32:09,280 --> 00:32:11,157
I was just trying to help you out.

472
00:32:11,320 --> 00:32:14,198
I said maybe you could do a few things
around here:

473
00:32:14,360 --> 00:32:16,920
file something,
deliver some things to the courthouse,

474
00:32:17,080 --> 00:32:20,152
just till you find another position.

475
00:32:20,360 --> 00:32:22,669
But you haven't done just that.

476
00:32:23,280 --> 00:32:26,317
You've flown in all directions.

477
00:32:27,040 --> 00:32:28,519
You've gotten yourself in situations

478
00:32:28,680 --> 00:32:32,992
that could've put you
in all kinds of trouble.

479
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:35,956
I can't be a part of that.

480
00:32:36,560 --> 00:32:38,551
Now, once again,

481
00:32:39,560 --> 00:32:42,358
there is no job.

482
00:32:43,200 --> 00:32:45,031
I'm sorry,

483
00:32:46,040 --> 00:32:48,076
but that's the end of it.

484
00:33:33,960 --> 00:33:35,439
Hello, Dr. Lindstrom.

485
00:33:35,600 --> 00:33:38,319
Oh, hello, Mr. Matlock.
Were you looking for me?

486
00:33:38,480 --> 00:33:40,596
No, I was just wandering around

487
00:33:40,760 --> 00:33:44,548
trying to get a fresh thought
on this case. I'm kind of stuck.

488
00:33:44,720 --> 00:33:47,518
Sometimes it helps, when you're stuck,
if you just kind of walk around.

489
00:33:47,680 --> 00:33:51,195
- Clears the head.
- I know. I do it all the time.

490
00:33:51,800 --> 00:33:56,112
Yeah. Miss Sutcliffe has Alex
for an alibi. I don't know if I buy that.

491
00:33:56,280 --> 00:33:59,113
And then Kimberly
is Josh Patterson's alibi.

492
00:33:59,280 --> 00:34:01,999
I don't know if I buy that.

493
00:34:02,360 --> 00:34:06,194
Boy, there's a lot of people
speaking up for one another.

494
00:34:06,360 --> 00:34:08,749
Well, I guess
it speaks for their commitment.

495
00:34:08,960 --> 00:34:10,678
Yeah.

496
00:34:11,400 --> 00:34:14,073
You're convinced Brett isn't guilty?

497
00:34:14,240 --> 00:34:18,119
I don't think he is. I really don't.

498
00:34:19,400 --> 00:34:23,439
Dr. Halvern used 60-minute tapes
to record those sessions.

499
00:34:23,600 --> 00:34:25,192
They don't make
50-minute cassettes.

500
00:34:25,360 --> 00:34:29,956
Yeah. Yeah. So he'd just let the tape
run out at the end of each session?

501
00:34:30,120 --> 00:34:31,792
That's correct.

502
00:34:32,280 --> 00:34:36,239
If his last appointment was 7:00,

503
00:34:36,400 --> 00:34:40,188
it's possible the tape was running

504
00:34:40,360 --> 00:34:42,828
when the killer
entered the therapy room.

505
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:45,878
But then that would mean that
he would have to have been murdered

506
00:34:46,040 --> 00:34:48,190
before 8:00.

507
00:34:48,360 --> 00:34:50,078
Well, anyway...

508
00:34:50,240 --> 00:34:53,789
- Wish I could've been more helpful.
- Oh, you were. You were.

509
00:34:53,960 --> 00:34:54,949
Dr. Lindstrom,

510
00:34:55,120 --> 00:34:59,033
I'm gonna need an expert witness
at court on this stuff.

511
00:34:59,200 --> 00:35:02,636
And since you're the only one I know,
I'm afraid you get the short straw.

512
00:35:02,800 --> 00:35:05,519
- Would you mind?
- Sure. When?

513
00:35:05,680 --> 00:35:07,989
- It's tomorrow.
- What time?

514
00:35:08,160 --> 00:35:10,310
- Nine.
- Oh, that's fine.

515
00:35:10,480 --> 00:35:12,118
Okay.

516
00:35:12,280 --> 00:35:16,239
The police sealed the therapy room,
didn't they, with the tapes inside?

517
00:35:16,400 --> 00:35:17,833
Yes, they did.

518
00:35:19,400 --> 00:35:22,119
Mrs. Sutcliffe told me yesterday

519
00:35:22,280 --> 00:35:25,192
that her session
started 1 5 minutes late.

520
00:35:25,360 --> 00:35:27,351
I think that's what she said.

521
00:35:27,520 --> 00:35:33,072
I wonder if her tape could've run
till 8:1 5.

522
00:35:34,360 --> 00:35:38,512
Well, thanks. Thanks.
And 9:00 sharp.

523
00:35:38,680 --> 00:35:41,399
Old Judge Cooksey's
bad about people coming late.

524
00:35:41,560 --> 00:35:45,712
- I'll be there.
- Thank you. Thank you.

525
00:35:50,200 --> 00:35:54,159
Dr. Lindstrom, you worked closely
with Dr. Halvern, didn't you?

526
00:35:54,320 --> 00:35:57,153
Yes. We worked together
for almost ten years.

527
00:35:57,320 --> 00:35:58,912
So you know
a lot about his practises?

528
00:35:59,080 --> 00:36:00,718
Yes.

529
00:36:01,600 --> 00:36:03,318
Let's...

530
00:36:03,920 --> 00:36:08,948
Let's pretend that I'm a patient
at your clinic.

531
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:11,989
Now, what happens first?

532
00:36:12,160 --> 00:36:14,720
We take a case history,
try to determine the problem,

533
00:36:14,880 --> 00:36:16,154
determine a therapy programme,

534
00:36:16,320 --> 00:36:18,834
and then you'd start sessions
with Dr. Halvern.

535
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:21,195
Dr. Halvern
recorded these sessions?

536
00:36:21,360 --> 00:36:22,679
Yes, he did.

537
00:36:22,840 --> 00:36:25,798
- Why?
- So we'd have absolute records.

538
00:36:28,160 --> 00:36:32,472
You knew Dr. Halvern personally
as well as professionally, didn't you?

539
00:36:33,040 --> 00:36:34,155
Yes.

540
00:36:34,320 --> 00:36:36,231
As I understand it, at one time,

541
00:36:36,400 --> 00:36:39,233
you and Dr. Halvern
were engaged to be married.

542
00:36:39,760 --> 00:36:41,318
Yes.

543
00:36:41,480 --> 00:36:43,755
But we decided
we didn't need artificial sanctions

544
00:36:43,920 --> 00:36:46,354
to justify our physical relationship.

545
00:36:49,160 --> 00:36:51,628
That's a pretty modern attitude.

546
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:54,598
Most people's perceptions about sex
are archaic.

547
00:36:55,840 --> 00:36:58,195
Did you know that Dr. Halvern
was having an affair

548
00:36:58,360 --> 00:37:01,591
with Mrs. Sutcliffe
and several others of the patients?

549
00:37:01,760 --> 00:37:04,069
I find that hard to believe.

550
00:37:04,240 --> 00:37:05,753
Well, I'll tell you what I believe.

551
00:37:05,920 --> 00:37:07,990
I believe that when you found out
about his affairs

552
00:37:08,160 --> 00:37:10,071
with Mrs. Sutcliffe and the others

553
00:37:10,240 --> 00:37:13,312
and you asked him to stop
and he wouldn't, you killed him.

554
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:16,674
That's absurd.

555
00:37:16,840 --> 00:37:18,831
Your Honour,
this is a preliminary hearing.

556
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:21,309
Mr. Matlock's speculations
have no place here.

557
00:37:21,480 --> 00:37:24,119
Your Honour,
this is a reasonable line of questioning

558
00:37:24,280 --> 00:37:27,078
that may very well save the court
time, expense

559
00:37:27,240 --> 00:37:29,993
and embarrassment
of trying an innocent man.

560
00:37:30,160 --> 00:37:33,436
I'm going to sustain the objection,
Mr. Matlock.

561
00:37:33,600 --> 00:37:34,919
Yes, sir.

562
00:37:35,080 --> 00:37:38,072
Do you know
who Bonnie McGrath is?

563
00:37:38,720 --> 00:37:42,474
- She's a television reporter, isn't she?
- Oh, yes.

564
00:37:42,640 --> 00:37:44,949
- Did you ever speak with her?
- No.

565
00:37:46,200 --> 00:37:49,112
Isn't it true that you're the one
who called Bonnie McGrath

566
00:37:49,280 --> 00:37:51,748
to tell her that Brett Cassidy
was staying at the clinic?

567
00:37:51,920 --> 00:37:52,909
No.

568
00:37:53,080 --> 00:37:57,119
Isn't it true that you told her
Brett Cassidy was staying at the clinic,

569
00:37:57,280 --> 00:37:59,589
in order to give him
an apparent motive for murder?

570
00:37:59,760 --> 00:38:01,910
- No.
- Objection.

571
00:38:02,080 --> 00:38:05,550
- Asked and answered.
- Sustained.

572
00:38:06,560 --> 00:38:12,510
Dr. Lindstrom, do you remember
our conversation yesterday

573
00:38:12,680 --> 00:38:16,878
about Mrs. Sutcliffe's last appointment
with Dr. Halvern?

574
00:38:17,840 --> 00:38:21,230
Yes. You said you thought
the last few minutes of her tape

575
00:38:21,400 --> 00:38:23,550
might contain footage of the murder.

576
00:38:24,080 --> 00:38:27,755
And Dr. Halvern
labelled all his cassettes, didn't he?

577
00:38:27,920 --> 00:38:30,070
Yes, with the patient's name
and date.

578
00:38:30,240 --> 00:38:33,198
So the cassette
that the court would be interested in

579
00:38:33,360 --> 00:38:38,480
would be labelled,
''Barbara Sutcliffe, February 2, 1 987''?

580
00:38:38,640 --> 00:38:39,834
That's right.

581
00:38:41,080 --> 00:38:43,071
Your Honour, at this time,

582
00:38:43,240 --> 00:38:47,438
in pursuant to the stipulation
we reached in chambers,

583
00:38:47,880 --> 00:38:51,793
I would like to play
and enter into evidence

584
00:38:53,600 --> 00:38:54,669
this video recording.

585
00:38:55,080 --> 00:38:56,274
Proceed.

586
00:38:57,040 --> 00:38:59,395
Now, Dr. Lindstrom,
I have to warn you,

587
00:38:59,560 --> 00:39:02,154
you have no idea what's on this tape.

588
00:39:02,680 --> 00:39:07,196
See, I wasn't quite truthful with you
yesterday when we talked.

589
00:39:08,360 --> 00:39:12,399
I told you that Barbara Sutcliffe's
last therapy session

590
00:39:12,560 --> 00:39:18,430
started 1 5 minutes late, which meant
that her tape would've run till 8:1 5,

591
00:39:18,600 --> 00:39:23,116
which means
if the killer entered the therapy room

592
00:39:23,280 --> 00:39:27,353
after the hour, 8:00,
to kill Dr. Halvern,

593
00:39:27,760 --> 00:39:33,198
that person would've been recorded
on videotape in the act.

594
00:39:33,360 --> 00:39:38,718
Which is why you had to get the tape,
because of that possibility.

595
00:39:39,320 --> 00:39:43,313
So, what we're going to see

596
00:39:43,480 --> 00:39:49,032
is a tape recorded
in Dr. Halvern's therapy room

597
00:39:49,200 --> 00:39:52,556
last night after we talked.

598
00:39:59,160 --> 00:40:02,709
It's a fake.
The cameras weren't on last night.

599
00:40:04,720 --> 00:40:06,153
How do you know?

600
00:40:08,680 --> 00:40:11,877
Because you didn't see
the red record light on the camera?

601
00:40:13,720 --> 00:40:18,191
What you don't know
is I had Mr. Fenton disconnect it.

602
00:40:20,720 --> 00:40:24,793
Now, let's see what you did
in the therapy room.

603
00:40:37,720 --> 00:40:40,996
We've blown up this part of the tape
optically.

604
00:40:41,160 --> 00:40:44,357
Dr. Lindstrom, would you read
the label on that cassette?

605
00:40:50,120 --> 00:40:52,680
Maybe you can't make it out
from there.

606
00:40:53,520 --> 00:40:58,913
It says, ''Barbara Sutcliffe,
February 2, 1 987.''

607
00:40:59,160 --> 00:41:01,958
The day Dr. Halvern was murdered.

608
00:41:02,120 --> 00:41:05,351
Only the killer
would've broken into the therapy room

609
00:41:05,520 --> 00:41:06,873
and would've taken that tape.

610
00:41:07,040 --> 00:41:08,712
Only the killer

611
00:41:08,880 --> 00:41:11,713
would've been afraid
of what was on it.

612
00:41:13,840 --> 00:41:15,990
No further questions.

613
00:41:17,800 --> 00:41:19,995
Your Honour, the defence moves

614
00:41:20,160 --> 00:41:23,072
for a complete dismissal
of all charges against Brett Cassidy.

615
00:41:23,240 --> 00:41:27,358
I'm inclined to grant the motion.
Does the prosecution object?

616
00:41:27,520 --> 00:41:28,873
No objection, Your Honour.

617
00:41:29,040 --> 00:41:31,508
Case dismissed.
This court is adjourned.

618
00:41:32,600 --> 00:41:34,989
Congratulations, Brett.
There they are.

619
00:41:35,160 --> 00:41:36,673
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

620
00:41:36,840 --> 00:41:38,876
Ben, I was a little worried
about Cassie,

621
00:41:39,040 --> 00:41:41,031
so I stopped by her school.
She's gone.

622
00:41:41,200 --> 00:41:44,715
Her roommate said she left for
the bus station about two hours ago.

623
00:41:44,920 --> 00:41:46,876
Where did her roommate
say she was going?

624
00:41:47,040 --> 00:41:48,393
She has no idea.

625
00:41:50,200 --> 00:41:53,317
Mama was right again.
Ain't nothing easy.

626
00:41:54,560 --> 00:41:56,198
Oh, here. Here.

627
00:41:56,360 --> 00:41:58,157
Gentlemen,
what do you say we go to my hotel

628
00:41:58,320 --> 00:42:00,550
and have dinner and celebrate, huh?

629
00:42:00,720 --> 00:42:04,156
You and Tyler go ahead.
I'll catch up to you later.

630
00:42:08,800 --> 00:42:11,109
<i>Shuttle service</i>
<i>to Atlanta International Airport</i>

631
00:42:11,280 --> 00:42:13,999
<i>now boarding at Gate 4.</i>

632
00:42:16,560 --> 00:42:18,312
Mind if I sit down?

633
00:42:20,120 --> 00:42:21,872
Okay.

634
00:42:35,120 --> 00:42:39,910
This bus-station coffee shop's
got the best cinnamon rolls in town.

635
00:42:44,520 --> 00:42:46,476
We won the case.

636
00:42:46,720 --> 00:42:48,676
Congratulations.

637
00:42:50,760 --> 00:42:52,955
So you're going on a trip.

638
00:42:53,240 --> 00:42:54,753
Yep.

639
00:42:55,720 --> 00:42:57,312
Dropped out of law school.

640
00:42:58,480 --> 00:42:59,959
Yep.

641
00:43:00,600 --> 00:43:02,716
That's a real shame.

642
00:43:03,960 --> 00:43:05,757
You could've made a fine lawyer
someday.

643
00:43:13,520 --> 00:43:17,149
I can be hard sometimes.

644
00:43:17,920 --> 00:43:19,558
Yeah.

645
00:43:20,880 --> 00:43:22,916
And stubborn.

646
00:43:25,720 --> 00:43:27,199
Yeah.

647
00:43:37,360 --> 00:43:39,476
<i>Transway bus to Chicago.</i>

648
00:43:39,640 --> 00:43:42,200
<i>All passengers</i>
<i>should now be boarding.</i>

649
00:43:43,600 --> 00:43:45,192
<i>Transway bus to Chicago.</i>

650
00:43:45,360 --> 00:43:48,272
<i>All passengers</i>
<i>should now be boarding.</i>

651
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:53,797
You know,

652
00:43:54,520 --> 00:44:00,709
I've had my law office
for a long time,

653
00:44:00,880 --> 00:44:04,668
and I plan to keep it
for a good long time still.

654
00:44:04,960 --> 00:44:09,112
I like it small,
just two or three people.

655
00:44:10,040 --> 00:44:15,034
If there was a young, intelligent,
energetic girl

656
00:44:15,200 --> 00:44:19,478
who, by the way,
did a lot toward winning this case,

657
00:44:19,640 --> 00:44:22,712
if she were to come back
to the office--

658
00:44:23,400 --> 00:44:26,949
She'd still have to mind
once in a while.

659
00:44:27,120 --> 00:44:31,750
And I probably could teach her
a few things.

660
00:44:33,600 --> 00:44:36,068
--you think she'd be interested?

661
00:44:36,480 --> 00:44:38,232
She might.

662
00:44:38,720 --> 00:44:41,188
It'd still be on a trial basis,

663
00:44:41,360 --> 00:44:46,195
and this time
there'd have to be some real rules.

664
00:44:46,360 --> 00:44:48,749
- Rules?
- Well,

665
00:44:49,440 --> 00:44:52,716
I am the senior partner in this outfit,

666
00:44:52,880 --> 00:44:58,159
and before she were to go running off,
talking to people,

667
00:44:58,320 --> 00:45:00,880
asking questions,
getting herself kidnapped,

668
00:45:01,040 --> 00:45:05,955
and things like that,
I think we should talk it over.

669
00:45:06,120 --> 00:45:07,758
Okay?

670
00:45:07,920 --> 00:45:09,592
Okay.

671
00:45:10,600 --> 00:45:12,158
Okay.

672
00:45:12,680 --> 00:45:14,716
Is that all?

673
00:45:14,880 --> 00:45:16,632
For now.

674
00:45:23,920 --> 00:45:26,070
You free for lunch?

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
